# Intro
Several fixed stars in a uniform, static, periodic glass box of gas, with
the ISRF (master switch on, propagation on or off) and no
photoionization, winds or supernovae. Tests the injection and propagation
of the photoelectric and Lyman-Werner fields with more than one source:

- with propagation off, the field injected by two stars equals, particle
  by particle, the sum of the fields of each star alone;
- with propagation on, the steady field of one, two and a lattice of stars
  satisfies the amplitude identity
  `sum_i m_i u_i / lambda_i = (1/c) sum_stars sum_j w_j L ext_j`
  (`lambda = 1/(kappa rho)` the dust absorption length, `w_j` the star's
  kernel weights, `ext_j` the receiver-side extinction);
- a dense lattice of stars (spacing `d = L/8`, under one absorption
  length in both bands) drives the M1 closure onto its isotropic branch
  away from the sources: the reduced flux `f = |F|/(c_hyp u)` stays small
  there. The check prints `d/lambda` per band.

The propagated field of two stars is not the sum of the single-star fields
where their beams overlap, since a two-moment closure merges crossing
beams; the check prints that difference without a bar.

## Runs
`run.sh` runs eight configurations into their own directories:
`injection_A`, `injection_B`, `injection_AB` (propagation off, four
steps), `A`, `B`, `AB` (propagation on, `Z/Zsun = 0.2`, one star at
`(3/8, 1/2, 1/2) L`, one at `(5/8, 1/2, 1/2) L`, both), `lattice`
(`8^3` stars at cell centres, `Z/Zsun = 0.1`) and `lattice_single` (one
star of that lattice). All stars are 29.7 Msun single stars on the gas
time step (`dt_max` below the young-star step cap).

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_0 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle
make -j
```

# Run
```
./run.sh
```
Environment overrides: `n_threads`, `swift` (binary path), `level`
(`N = (2**level)**3` gas particles), `gas_density` (atom/cm^3), `gas_mass`
(Msun), `star_mass`, `n_side`, `Z_pair`, `Z_lattice`, `time_end`, `dt_max`,
`delta_time` (propagation runs), and `runs` (a subset of the eight names).
A finer `level` at fixed box needs `gas_mass` divided by 8 per level and
`dt_max` halved per level (keep it slightly above the wanted power-of-two
bin, which SWIFT floors to), so that `c_hyp dt/h` and the number of
relaxation times stay the same.

# Checking
```
python3 isrf_multi_source_superposition_check.py [--dir runs_directory]
```
`run.sh` runs it at the end. It exits nonzero if any gate fails; a
non-finite value fails its gate. Gates, per band:

- per-particle superposition with propagation off (stars `L/16` apart,
  overlapping kernels): `|u_AB - u_A - u_B|` at most `1e-5 (u_A + u_B)`
  plus four float32 epsilons of the peak field, the float32 error of the
  kernel polynomial near its support radius;
- amplitude identity of `A` and `B` within 0.10, and of `AB` within
  `|e_A - e_B|/2 + 3 sigma` of `(e_A + e_B)/2`, `sigma` the scatter of the
  single-star errors over the last four snapshots;
- amplitude identity of `lattice` within `|e| + 3 sigma` of
  `lattice_single`;
- median reduced flux outside every star's kernel in `lattice` at most
  0.18, where the M1 Eddington factor is within 5% of the isotropic 1/3,
  with every particle in that median lit.

It also prints the lattice's spatial scatter of `u` next to the scatter
of the continuum free-streaming and diffusive lattice sums, and the
single-star reduced flux at the same distances.
